 wealth.","Throughout history, the Gold Standard has been a point of contention, celebrated for its ability to promote economic stability while criticized for its inherent limitations.","Its adoption marked a pivotal shift in global finance, influencing the economic policies of nations and reshaping the landscape of international commerce.","As countries embraced this standard, they navigated a complex interplay of economic forces, often leading to profound implications for their financial systems.","In this exploration of the Gold Standard, we will delve into its historical origins, examine its implementation across key nations, and analyze the economic repercussions it had on global trade.","By understanding the Gold Standard's legacy, we can better appreciate its enduring significance in the context of modern monetary policy and economic theory.","As we move forward, it is essential to recognize both its strengths and weaknesses, as these factors continue to inform discussions about currency systems today."],detected_special_symbols:[],detected_non_latin_languages:[],request_message:"I. Introduction to the Gold Standard\nThe Gold Standard represents one of the most significant monetary systems in history, embodying a unique relationship between currency and precious metals. Under this system, the value of a country's currency is directly linked to a specific amount of gold, establishing a fixed exchange rate that creates stability in international trade. This framework not only facilitated cross-border transactions but also provided a sense of security for investors and consumers alike, as the intrinsic value of gold served as a reliable measure of wealth.\n\nThroughout history, the Gold Standard has been a point of contention, celebrated for its ability to promote economic stability while criticized for its inherent limitations. Its adoption marked a pivotal shift in global finance, influencing the economic policies of nations and reshaping the landscape of international commerce. As countries embraced this standard, they navigated a complex interplay of economic forces, often leading to profound implications for their financial systems.\n\nIn this exploration of the Gold Standard, we will delve into its historical origins, examine its implementation across key nations, and analyze the economic repercussions it had on global trade. By understanding the Gold Standard's legacy, we can better appreciate its enduring significance in the context of modern monetary policy and economic theory. As we move forward, it is essential to recognize both its strengths and weaknesses, as these factors continue to inform discussions about currency systems today.",reaction:0,plagiarism_check_execution:null,created_at:"2025-02-18T12:36:49.028280057Z",updated_at:"2025-02-18T12:36:49.028280199Z",demo_mode:!0,free_humanize_count:0};const l=t.IsShowedDetectorTutorial="is_showed_detector_tutorial";t.IsSkippedDetectorTutorial="is_skipped_detector_tutorial",t.getAiDetectorHighlightConfig=e=>({[o.HIGHLIGHT.AI_DETECTOR_TEXT_INPUT]:{title:e("highlight:ai_detector.text_input.title","AI Text Highlights"),text:e("highlight:ai_detector.text_input.text","Selected AI-generated sentence is highlighted in yellow, the rest — in blue"),placement:"right-start",buttonText:e("general:next","Next"),onShowCallBack:()=>{i.default.trackEvent("tutorial - show tip",{tool:a,tip_number:2})},onSubmitCallback:()=>{i.default.trackEvent("tutorial - click next",{tool:a,tip_number:2})}},[o.HIGHLIGHT.AI_DETECTOR_NAVIGATOR]:{title:e("highlight:ai_detector.navigator.title","Navigate The Text"),text:e("highlight:ai_detector.navigator.text","These buttons allow you to highlight the next or previous sentence that is probably AI-generated. When the text is partially flagged as AI-generated, manually editing highlighted parts can be highly beneficial."),placement:"bottom-start",buttonText:e("general:next","Next"),onShowCallBack:()=>{i.default.trackEvent("tutorial - show tip",{tool:a,tip_number:3})},onSubmitCallback:()=>{i.default.trackEvent("tutorial - click next",{tool:a,tip_number:3})}},[o.HIGHLIGHT.AI_DETECTOR_HUMANIZE_BUTTON]:{title:e("highlight:ai_detector.humanize_button.title","Humanize Text"),text:e("highlight:ai_detector.humanize_button.text","Use this feature to decrease the probability of the text being flagged by AI detection software"),placement:"bottom-start",buttonText:e("general:next","Next"),onShowCallBack:()=>{i.default.trackEvent("tutorial - show tip",{tool:a,tip_number:4})},onSubmitCallback:()=>{i.default.trackEvent("tutorial - click next",{tool:a,tip_number:4})}},[o.HIGHLIGHT.AI_DETECTOR_FACT_CHECK_BUTTON]:{title:e("highlight:ai_detector.fact_check_button.title","Fact Check"),text:e("highlight:ai_detector.fact_check_button.text","Get a detailed fact-check report of the text to fix possible issues in this regard"),placement:"bottom-end",buttonText:e("general:next","Next"),onShowCallBack:()=>{i.default.trackEvent("tutorial - show tip",{tool:a,tip_number:5})},onSubmitCallback:()=>{i.default.trackEvent("tutorial - click next",{tool:a,tip_number:5})}},[o.HIGHLIGHT.AI_DETECTOR_DETAILED_REPORT_BUTTON]:{title:e("highlight:ai_detector.detailed_report_button.title","Detailed Report"),text:e("highlight:ai_detector.detailed_report_button.text","Get a document with complete information about the text regarding AI content inside"),placement:"bottom-start",buttonText:e("general:next","Next"),onShowCallBack:()=>{i.default.trackEvent("tutorial - show tip",{tool:a,tip_number:6})},onSubmitCallback:()=>{i.default.trackEvent("tutorial - click next",{tool:a,tip_number:6})}},[o.HIGHLIGHT.AI_DETECTOR_TIPS_BUTTON]:{title:e("highlight:ai_detector.tips_button.title","Tips To Lower AI Score"),text:e("highlight:ai_detector.tips_button.text","Try using our proven tips to eliminate AI traces when humanized text still gets flagged as AI-generated"),placement:"bottom-end",buttonText:e("general:finish","Finish"),onShowCallBack:()=>{i.default.trackEvent("tutorial - show tip",{tool:a,tip_number:7})},onSubmitCallback:e=>{e({highlights:{[l]:!0}}),i.default.trackEvent("tutorial - finished",{tool:a})}}})},26186:(e,t,n)=>{"use strict";Object.defineProperty(t,"__esModule",{value:!0}),t.getTextSpecialSymbols=t.getDetectorWordsBalance=t.getDetectorInputLimits=t.getDetectionStage=void 0;var r=n(53134);t.getDetectionStage=e=>{const t=Object.entries(r.DETECTION_EDGE).sort(((e,t)=>{let[,n]=e,[,r]=t;return r-n})).find((t=>{let[,n]=t;return e>=n}));return t?t[0]:r.DETECTION_STAGE.FULLY_HUMAN},t.getTextSpecialSymbols=e=>{const t=e.match(/[*#]/g);return t?[...new Set(t)]:[]},t.getDetectorWordsBalance=()=>8e4,t.getDetectorInputLimits=e=>({minCount:50,maxCount:e.isNotPremium?25e3:5e4})},90985:(e,t)=>{"use strict";Object.defineProperty(t,"__esModule",{value:!0}),t.EXAMPLE_RESPONSE=t.DETECTOR_VALID_FILE_EXTENSIONS=t.DETECTOR_MAX_FILE_SIZE=t.DETECTION_STAGE=t.DETECTION_EDGE=t.AiDetectorTitle=t.AiDetectorExampleShowedKey=void 0,t.DETECTOR_MAX_FILE_SIZE=2e7,t.DETECTOR_VALID_FILE_EXTENSIONS=["pdf","docx","txt"];let n=t.DETECTION_STAGE=function(e){return e.FULLY_HUMAN="fully_human",e.MOSTLY_HUMAN="mostly_human",e.MEDIUM="medium",e.MOSTLY_AI="mostly_ai",e.FULLY_AI="fully_ai",e}({});t.AiDetectorTitle="AI Content Detector",t.AiDetectorExampleShowedKey="ai_detector_example_showed",t.DETECTION_EDGE={[n.FULLY_AI]:100,[n.MOSTLY_AI]:61,[n.MEDIUM]:31,[n.MOSTLY_HUMAN]:1,[n.FULLY_HUMAN]:0},t.EXAMPLE_RESPONSE={id:"example_response",summary:"The Gold Standard as a significant historical monetary system.",report_url:"",fake_percentage:97,detected_sentences:["The Gold Standard represents one of the most significant monetary systems in history, embodying a unique relationship between currency and precious metals.","Under this system, the value of a country's currency is directly linked to a specific amount of gold, establishing a fixed exchange rate that creates stability in international trade.","This framework not only facilitated cross-border transactions but also provided a sense of security for investors and consumers alike, as the intrinsic value of gold served as a reliable measure of wealth.","Throughout history, the Gold Standard has been a point of contention, celebrated for its ability to promote economic stability while criticized for its inherent limitations.","Its adoption marked a pivotal shift in global finance, influencing the economic policies of nations and reshaping the landscape of international commerce.","As countries embraced this standard, they navigated a complex interplay of economic forces, often leading to profound implications for their financial systems.","In this exploration of the Gold Standard, we will delve into its historical origins, examine its implementation across key nations, and analyze the economic repercussions it had on global trade.","By understanding the Gold Standard's legacy, we can better appreciate its enduring significance in the context of modern monetary policy and economic theory.","As we move forward, it is essential to recognize both its strengths and weaknesses, as these factors continue to inform discussions about currency systems today."],detected_special_symbols:[],detected_non_latin_languages:[],request_message:"I. Introduction to the Gold Standard\nThe Gold Standard represents one of the most significant monetary systems in history, embodying a unique relationship between currency and precious metals. Under this system, the value of a country's currency is directly linked to a specific amount of gold, establishing a fixed exchange rate that creates stability in international trade. This framework not only facilitated cross-border transactions but also provided a sense of security for investors and consumers alike, as the intrinsic value of gold served as a reliable measure of wealth.\n\nThroughout history, the Gold Standard has been a point of contention, celebrated for its ability to promote economic stability while criticized for its inherent limitations. Its adoption marked a pivotal shift in global finance, influencing the economic policies of nations and reshaping the landscape of international commerce. As countries embraced this standard, they navigated a complex interplay of economic forces, often leading to profound implications for their financial systems.\n\nIn this exploration of the Gold Standard, we will delve into its historical origins, examine its implementation across key nations, and analyze the economic repercussions it had on global trade. By understanding the Gold Standard's legacy, we can better appreciate its enduring significance in the context of modern monetary policy and economic theory. As we move forward, it is essential to recognize both its strengths and weaknesses, as these factors continue to inform discussions about currency systems today.",reaction:0,plagiarism_check_execution:null,created_at:"2025-02-18T12:36:49.028280057Z",updated_at:"2025-02-18T12:36:49.028280199Z",demo_mode:!0,free_humanize_count:0}},66419:(e,t,n)=>{"use strict";Object.defineProperty(t,"__esModule",{value:!0}),t.getDetectorWordsBalance=t.getDetectorLoadingTime=t.getDetectorInputLimits=t.getDetectionStage=t.calculateDetectorLoadingTime=void 0;var r=n(90985),o=n(31521);t.getDetectionStage=e=>{const t=Object.entries(r.DETECTION_EDGE).sort(((e,t)=>{let[,n]=e,[,r]=t;return r-n})).find((t=>{let[,n]=t;return e>=n}));return t?t[0]:r.DETECTION_STAGE.FULLY_HUMAN};const i=e=>{const t=e.length;if(t>15e4)return 6e4;const n=358e-6*t+5.9;return 1e3*Math.round(n)};t.getDetectorLoadingTime=i,t.calculateDetectorLoadingTime=e=>{const t=i(e.response_text);if(e.is_plagiarism_included){const n=(0,o.getPlagiarismLoadingTime)(e.response_text);return Math.max(t,n)}return t},t.getDetectorWordsBalance=()=>8e4,t.getDetectorInputLimits=e=>({minCount:50,maxCount:e.isNotPremium?25e3:5e4})},50939:(e,t,n)=>{"use strict";var r=n(24994);Object.defineProperty(t,"__esModule",{value:!0}),t.getHumanizerModeV2Options=t.getAiHumanizerHighlightConfig=t.IsShowedAiHumanizerTutorial=t.HUMANIZER_MODE_V2=t.EXAMPLE_RESPONSE=t.CLICK_TOGGLER_ANALYTIC_NAMES=t.AiHumanizerTitle=void 0;var o=n(44297),i=n(64105),a=r(n(62893));const s=t.AiHumanizerTitle="AI Text Humanizer";let l=t.HUMANIZER_MODE_V2=function(e){return e.Human="sound_human",e.Auto="auto",e.Detectors="bypass_detectors",e}({});t.getHumanizerModeV2Options=e=>({[l.Human]:{value:"sound_human",text:e("tools:ai_humanizer_v2.form_mode_options_text[0]","Sound Human")},[l.Auto]:{value:"auto",text:e("tools:ai_humanizer_v2.form_mode_options_text[1]","Auto")},[l.Detectors]:{value:"bypass_detectors",text:e("tools:ai_humanizer_v2.form_mode_options_text[2]","Bypass Detectors")}}),t.CLICK_TOGGLER_ANALYTIC_NAMES={[l.Auto]:"ai humanizer - select auto goal",[l.Human]:"ai humanizer - select sound human goal",[l.Detectors]:"ai humanizer - select bypass detectors goal"},t.EXAMPLE_RESPONSE={id:"example_response",mode:"Auto",language:"English",mixed_languages:!1,reaction:i.REACTION.NONE,summary:"Critique of the Dow Jones Industrial Average.",request_message:"I. Introduction to the Gold Standard\n\nThe Gold Standard represents one of the most significant monetary systems in history, embodying a unique relationship between currency and precious metals. Under this system, the value of a country's currency is directly linked to a specific amount of gold, establishing a fixed exchange rate that creates stability in international trade. This framework not only facilitated cross-border transactions but also provided a sense of security for investors and consumers alike, as the intrinsic value of gold served as a reliable measure of wealth.\n\nThroughout history, the Gold Standard has been a point of contention, celebrated for its ability to promote economic stability while criticized for its inherent limitations. Its adoption marked a pivotal shift in global finance, influencing the economic policies of nations and reshaping the landscape of international commerce. As countries embraced this standard, they navigated a complex interplay of economic forces, often leading to profound implications for their financial systems.\n\nIn this exploration of the Gold Standard, we will delve into its historical origins, examine its implementation across key nations, and analyze the economic repercussions it had on global trade. By understanding the Gold Standard's legacy, we can better appreciate its enduring significance in the context of modern monetary policy and economic theory. As we move forward, it is essential to recognize both its strengths and weaknesses, as these factors continue to inform discussions about currency systems today.",response_message:"I. The Gold Standard Explained\n\nThe Gold Standard is one of the most important monetary systems in history, and it had a very unique relationship between the currency and precious metals. In this system, a country's currency has a basic value linked to a certain amount of gold, enabling a fixed exchange rate that ensures stability in international trade. It provided a bridge for cross-border transactions and a cushion for investors and consumers alike, as gold, after all, is a universal measure of wealth.\n\nThe Gold Standard, historically, has been a double-edged sword, commended for fostering economic stability but derided for its restrictions. Its acceptance ushered in a significant change in international finance, shaping the policies of governments and transforming the landscape of world trade. Countries that adopted this standard grappled with a delicate balance of economic forces, often resulting in significant consequences for their financial systems.\n\nJoin me here in this exploration of the Gold Standard as we look back at its birth, a look into how it was implemented in major nations, and the impact on world trade. After delving into the historical account of the Gold Standard, one gains a deeper understanding of its lasting impact on contemporary monetary policy and economic thought. With that being said, we must also take into account both the pros and cons, as elements of that type of system are still prevalent in conversations relating to modern-day currency systems as well.",created_at:"2025-02-13T14:05:15.303906Z",updated_at:"2025-02-13T14:05:18.0498Z",ai_edit_items:[],ai_detector:null,ai_detector_execution:null,demo_mode:!0};const c=t.IsShowedAiHumanizerTutorial="is_showed_ai_humanizer_tutorial";t.getAiHumanizerHighlightConfig=e=>({[o.HIGHLIGHT.AI_HUMANIZER_GOAL_SOUND_HUMAN]:{title:e("highlight:ai_humanizer.sound_human.title","Sound Human"),text:e("highlight:ai_humanizer.sound_human.text","Light humanization mode aimed to make text appear as human written but not necessarily pass the strictest detectors"),placement:"bottom-start",buttonText:e("general:next","Next"),onShowCallBack:()=>{a.default.trackEvent("tutorial - show tip",{tool:s,tip_number:2})},onSubmitCallback:()=>{a.default.trackEvent("tutorial - click next",{tool:s,tip_number:2})}},[o.HIGHLIGHT.AI_HUMANIZER_GOAL_AUTO]:{title:e("highlight:ai_humanizer.goal_auto.title","Auto"),text:e("highlight:ai_humanizer.goal_auto.text","The system detects the best mode for a text to achieve a balanced result"),placement:"bottom",buttonText:e("general:next","Next"),onShowCallBack:()=>{a.default.trackEvent("tutorial - show tip",{tool:s,tip_number:3})},onSubmitCallback:()=>{a.default.trackEvent("tutorial - click next",{tool:s,tip_number:3})}},[o.HIGHLIGHT.AI_HUMANIZER_GOAL_BYPASS_DETECTOR]:{title:e("highlight:ai_humanizer.bypass_detector.title","Bypass Detectors"),text:e("highlight:ai_humanizer.bypass_detector.text","Aggressive setting with the primary goal of bypassing the strictest detectors. Caution: sometimes, this may bring unusual results or grammar mistakes, so double-checking the text is recommended."),placement:"bottom-end",buttonText:e("general:next","Next"),onShowCallBack:()=>{a.default.trackEvent("tutorial - show tip",{tool:s,tip_number:4})},onSubmitCallback:()=>{a.default.trackEvent("tutorial - click next",{tool:s,tip_number:4})}},[o.HIGHLIGHT.AI_HUMANIZER_DETECT_AI]:{title:e("highlight:ai_humanizer.detect_ai.title","Detect AI"),text:e("highlight:ai_humanizer.detect_ai.text","Scan the text to double-check if it is being flagged as AI-generated"),placement:"top-start",buttonText:e("general:next","Next"),onShowCallBack:()=>{a.default.trackEvent("tutorial - show tip",{tool:s,tip_number:5})},onSubmitCallback:()=>{a.default.trackEvent("tutorial - click next",{tool:s,tip_number:5})}},[o.HIGHLIGHT.AI_HUMANIZER_AI_EDIT]:{title:e("highlight:ai_humanizer.ai_edit.title","AI Edit"),text:e("humanizer.ai_edit.text","This feature allows you to ask AI to do different things with text, such as summarize, change tone, or do anything else you ask."),placement:"top-start",buttonText:e("general:finish","Finish"),onShowCallBack:()=>{a.default.trackEvent("tutorial - show tip",{tool:s,tip_number:6})},onSubmitCallback:e=>{e({highlights:{[c]:!0}}),a.default.trackEvent("tutorial - finished",{tool:s})}}})},49440:(e,t,n)=>{"use strict";var r=n(24994);Object.defineProperty(t,"__esModule",{value:!0}),t.getHumanizerModeV2Options=t.getHumanizerAiEditOptions=t.HUMANIZER_VALID_FILE_EXTENSIONS=t.HUMANIZER_MODE_V2=t.HUMANIZER_MAX_FILE_SIZE=t.EXAMPLE_RESPONSE=t.CLICK_TOGGLER_ANALYTIC_NAMES=t.AiHumanizerTitle=t.AiHumanizerExampleShowedKey=void 0;var o=r(n(96540)),i=n(64105),a=n(87701),s=n(15217),l=n(10480),c=n(70834),u=n(97440),d=n(85101),p=n(2804),f=n(31278),g=n(72394),M=n(81991),m=n(99083);t.AiHumanizerTitle="AI Text Humanizer",t.AiHumanizerExampleShowedKey="ai_humanizer_example_showed",t.HUMANIZER_MAX_FILE_SIZE=2e7,t.HUMANIZER_VALID_FILE_EXTENSIONS=["docx","pdf","txt"];let h=t.HUMANIZER_MODE_V2=function(e){return e.Human="sound_human",e.Auto="auto",e.Detectors="bypass_detectors",e}({});t.getHumanizerModeV2Options=e=>({[h.Human]:{value:"sound_human",text:e("tools:ai_humanizer_v2.form_mode_options_text[0]","Sound Human")},[h.Auto]:{value:"auto",text:e("tools:ai_humanizer_v2.form_mode_options_text[1]","Auto")},[h.Detectors]:{value:"bypass_detectors",text:e("tools:ai_humanizer_v2.form_mode_options_text[2]","Bypass Detectors")}}),t.CLICK_TOGGLER_ANALYTIC_NAMES={[h.Auto]:"ai humanizer - select auto goal",[h.Human]:"ai humanizer - select sound human goal",[h.Detectors]:"ai humanizer - select bypass detectors goal"},t.EXAMPLE_RESPONSE={id:"example_response",mode:"Auto",language:"English",mixed_languages:!1,reaction:i.REACTION.NONE,summary:"Critique of the Dow Jones Industrial Average.",request_message:"I. Introduction to the Gold Standard\n\nThe Gold Standard represents one of the most significant monetary systems in history, embodying a unique relationship between currency and precious metals. Under this system, the value of a country's currency is directly linked to a specific amount of gold, establishing a fixed exchange rate that creates stability in international trade. This framework not only facilitated cross-border transactions but also provided a sense of security for investors and consumers alike, as the intrinsic value of gold served as a reliable measure of wealth.\n\nThroughout history, the Gold Standard has been a point of contention, celebrated for its ability to promote economic stability while criticized for its inherent limitations. Its adoption marked a pivotal shift in global finance, influencing the economic policies of nations and reshaping the landscape of international commerce. As countries embraced this standard, they navigated a complex interplay of economic forces, often leading to profound implications for their financial systems.\n\nIn this exploration of the Gold Standard, we will delve into its historical origins, examine its implementation across key nations, and analyze the economic repercussions it had on global trade. By understanding the Gold Standard's legacy, we can better appreciate its enduring significance in the context of modern monetary policy and economic theory. As we move forward, it is essential to recognize both its strengths and weaknesses, as these factors continue to inform discussions about currency systems today.",response_message:"I. The Gold Standard Explained\n\nThe Gold Standard is one of the most important monetary systems in history, and it had a very unique relationship between the currency and precious metals. In this system, a country's currency has a basic value linked to a certain amount of gold, enabling a fixed exchange rate that ensures stability in international trade. It provided a bridge for cross-border transactions and a cushion for investors and consumers alike, as gold, after all, is a universal measure of wealth.\n\nThe Gold Standard, historically, has been a double-edged sword, commended for fostering economic stability but derided for its restrictions. Its acceptance ushered in a significant change in international finance, shaping the policies of governments and transforming the landscape of world trade. Countries that adopted this standard grappled with a delicate balance of economic forces, often resulting in significant consequences for their financial systems.\n\nJoin me here in this exploration of the Gold Standard as we look back at its birth, a look into how it was implemented in major nations, and the impact on world trade. After delving into the historical account of the Gold Standard, one gains a deeper understanding of its lasting impact on contemporary monetary policy and economic thought. With that being said, we must also take into account both the pros and cons, as elements of that type of system are still prevalent in conversations relating to modern-day currency systems as well.",created_at:"2025-02-13T14:05:15.303906Z",updated_at:"2025-02-13T14:05:18.0498Z",ai_edit_items:[],ai_detector_execution:null,demo_mode:!0},t.getHumanizerAiEditOptions=e=>[{text:e("general:humanize","Humanize"),value:"humanize",icon:o.default.createElement(u.ReactComponent,null)},{text:e("general:improve","Improve"),value:e("ai_edit_options:values[0]","improve this text"),icon:o.default.createElement(d.ReactComponent,null)},{text:e("general:shorter","Shorter"),value:e("ai_edit_options:values[2]","make this text shorter"),icon:o.default.createElement(f.ReactComponent,null)},{text:e("general:longer","Longer"),value:e("ai_edit_options:values[4]","make this text longer"),icon:o.default.createElement(p.ReactComponent,null)},{text:e("general:change_tone","Change Tone"),value:e("ai_edit_options:values[8]","change tone of voice of this text to [paste new tone]"),icon:o.default.createElement(M.ReactComponent,null)},{text:e("general:detect_ai","Detect Ai"),value:"detect ai",icon:o.default.createElement(c.ReactComponent,null)},{text:e("general:check_plagiarism","Check Plagiarism"),value:"check plagiarism",icon:o.default.createElement(s.ReactComponent,null)},{text:e("general:summarize","Summarize"),value:e("ai_edit_options:values[6]","summarize this text"),icon:o.default.createElement(g.ReactComponent,null)},{text:e("general:change_audience","Change Audience"),value:e("ai_edit_options:values[10]","rewrite text for the next audience [paste new audience]"),icon:o.default.createElement(a.ReactComponent,null)},{text:e("general:continue_writing","Continue Writing"),value:e("ai_edit_options:values[1]","continue writing this text"),icon:o.default.createElement(l.ReactComponent,null)},{text:e("general:explain","Explain"),value:e("ai_edit_options:values[9]","explain this text"),icon:o.default.createElement(d.ReactComponent,null)},{text:e("general:translate","Translate"),value:e("ai_edit_options:values[11]","translate this text to: [output language]"),icon:o.default.createElement(m.ReactComponent,null)}]},31724:(e,t,n)=>{"use strict";var r=n(24994);Object.defineProperty(t,"__esModule",{value:!0}),t.getHumanizerWordsBalance=t.getHumanizerLoadingTime=t.getHumanizerInputLimits=t.calculateHumanizerLoadingTime=void 0;var o=r(n(17790)),i=n(92321),a=n(66419),s=n(49440);const l=(e,t)=>{var n;const r=navigator.language.split("-")[0],a=(null===(n=o.default.find((e=>{let{code:t}=e;return t===r})))||void 0===n?void 0:n.language)||"English",l=(0,i.getWordsCount)(e),c=t===s.HUMANIZER_MODE_V2.Human,u={human:{english:{maxTime:38e3,coef:.0133,threshold:14.2},nonEnglish:{maxTime:23e4,coef:.117,threshold:17.4}},nonHuman:{english:{maxTime:27e3,coef:.0103,threshold:8.45},nonEnglish:{maxTime:215e3,coef:.113,threshold:11.9}}},{maxTime:d,coef:p,threshold:f}="English"===a?c?u.human.english:u.nonHuman.english:c?u.human.nonEnglish:u.nonHuman.nonEnglish;if(l>1800)return d;const g=p*l+f;return Math.round(1e3*g)};t.getHumanizerLoadingTime=l,t.calculateHumanizerLoadingTime=e=>{const t=l(e.response_text,e.mode);return e.is_detector_included?(0,a.getDetectorLoadingTime)(e.response_text)+t:t},t.getHumanizerWordsBalance=()=>8e4,t.getHumanizerInputLimits=()=>({minCount:65,maxCount:1800})},51833:(e,t,n)=>{"use strict";var r=n(24994);Object.defineProperty(t,"__esModule",{value:!0}),t.getParaphraserHighlightConfig=t.ParaphraserTitle=t.IsShowedParaphraserTutorial=t.EXAMPLE_RESPONSE=void 0;var o=n(44297),i=n(64105),a=r(n(62893));const s=t.ParaphraserTitle="Paraphrase Text",l=(t.EXAMPLE_RESPONSE={id:"example_response",text:"A gold standard refers to a monetary framework where the primary unit of account is tied to a specific amount of gold. This system served as the foundation for international finance from the 1870s until the early 1920s, and again from the late 1920s through 1932, continuing until 1971 when the United States ended the convertibility of its dollar into gold, thereby concluding the Bretton Woods arrangement. Despite this shift, many countries continue to maintain significant gold reserves.\n\nHistorically, both the silver standard and bimetallism were more prevalent than the gold standard. The transition to a global monetary system anchored in gold was influenced by chance events, network effects, and historical precedents. Notably, Great Britain inadvertently established a de facto gold standard in 1717 when Isaac Newton, who was then in charge of the Royal Mint, set an exchange rate that undervalued silver compared to gold, leading to the withdrawal of silver coins from circulation. As Great Britain emerged as a dominant financial and trade power during the 19th century, other nations increasingly adopted its monetary practices.\n\nThe gold standard saw significant decline during the Great Depression, although it was later reintroduced in a limited capacity as part of the post-World War II Bretton Woods system. Its abandonment was largely due to its tendency towards instability and the limitations it placed on government action; fixed exchange rates restricted governments' ability to implement expansionary measures aimed at reducing unemployment during economic downturns.",reaction:i.REACTION.NONE,symbols:1660,words:248,created_at:"2025-02-18T18:50:06.686461Z",updated_at:"2025-02-18T18:50:11.831728Z",ai_edit_items:[],children:[],user_inputs:{original_text:"A gold standard is a monetary system in which the standard economic unit of account is based on a fixed quantity of gold. The gold standard was the basis for the international monetary system from the 1870s to the early 1920s, and from the late 1920s to 1932 as well as from 1944 until 1971 when the United States unilaterally terminated convertibility of the US dollar to gold, effectively ending the Bretton Woods system.Many states nonetheless hold substantial gold reserves.\n\nHistorically, the silver standard and bimetallism have been more common than the gold standard.The shift to an international monetary system based on a gold standard reflected accident, network externalities, and path dependence.Great Britain accidentally adopted a de facto gold standard in 1717 when Isaac Newton, then-master of the Royal Mint, set the exchange rate of silver to gold too low, thus causing silver coins to go out of circulation. As Great Britain became the world's leading financial and commercial power in the 19th century, other states increasingly adopted Britain's monetary system.\n\nThe gold standard was largely abandoned during the Great Depression before being reinstated in a limited form as part of the post-World War II Bretton Woods system. The gold standard was abandoned due to its propensity for volatility, as well as the constraints it imposed on governments: by retaining a fixed exchange rate, governments were hamstrung in engaging in expansionary policies to, for example, reduce unemployment during economic recessions.",tone_of_voice:"Neutral",output_counter:1,paraphrase_level:"minimum"},demo_mode:!0},t.IsShowedParaphraserTutorial="is_showed_paraphraser_tutorial");t.getParaphraserHighlightConfig=e=>({[o.HIGHLIGHT.PARAPHRASER_LEVEL_MIN]:{title:e("highlight:paraphraser.level_min.title","Minimum Paraphrase Level"),text:e("highlight:paraphraser.level_min.text","Slight changes to the text with minor deviations from the original"),placement:"top-start",buttonText:e("general:next","Next"),onShowCallBack:()=>{a.default.trackEvent("tutorial - show tip",{tool:s,tip_number:1})},onSubmitCallback:()=>{a.default.trackEvent("tutorial - click next",{tool:s,tip_number:1})}},[o.HIGHLIGHT.PARAPHRASER_LEVEL_RECOMMENDED]:{title:e("highlight:paraphraser.level_recommended.title","Recommended"),text:e("highlight:paraphraser.level_recommended.text","Balanced mode with moderate changes to the text"),buttonText:e("general:next","Next"),onShowCallBack:()=>{a.default.trackEvent("tutorial - show tip",{tool:s,tip_number:2})},onSubmitCallback:()=>{a.default.trackEvent("tutorial - click next",{tool:s,tip_number:2})}},[o.HIGHLIGHT.PARAPHRASER_LEVEL_MAX]:{title:e("highlight:paraphraser.level_max.title","Maximum"),text:e("highlight:paraphraser.level_max.text","Substantial paraphrasing of the text, making the result very different from the initial text but maintaining the original meaning"),placement:"top-end",buttonText:e("general:next","Next"),onShowCallBack:()=>{a.default.trackEvent("tutorial - show tip",{tool:s,tip_number:3})}